"""Port the design package's inner pages into app/nxm/<route>.

Runs the package's OWN builders (source/build_page.py, source/build_games2.py)
unchanged, intercepting only their last step: instead of base64-inlining
images and writing dist/*.html, images are saved to public/nxm/a/ and the
assembled page is captured. So the markup/CSS/JS is exactly what was
approved; the owner's identity changes are then applied (nxmlib.py).

    python3 tools/nxm/port_pages.py            # every page
    python3 tools/nxm/port_pages.py vps pricing

Outputs per page (generated — edit this script, never the outputs):
  app/nxm/_pages/<slug>/page.css     every selector scoped to .nxm-p-<slug>
  app/nxm/_pages/<slug>/content.ts   title/description + page markup
  app/nxm/_pages/<slug>/script.ts    the page's script (nav, reveal, page JS)
  app/nxm/<route>/page.tsx           the route
Shared: public/nxm/a/<hash>.<ext> (images, de-duplicated across pages)
"""
